{"name":"Nairobi","slug":"nairobi","region":"Africa","lat":-1.29,"lon":36.82,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Nairobi has warmed by about 0.3 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 2.2 °C in all. There is a modest but consistent El Niño signal on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding Sep–Nov, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 50% of a normal year-to-year swing, a noticeable tilt, though ordinary variability can easily outweigh it, roughly as much warmth as 7 years of the long-term trend. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a wetter season with more rainy days, and this year's shift is substantial. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.6 points per decade, roughly 5 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 90% chance), about 0.9 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a wetter-than-normal season is more likely than not (about 65%), and a more humid season than normal is more likely than not (about 60%). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":19.6898,"trend_per_decade":0.2904,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":2.1782,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0985,"enso_p":0.0818,"confidence":"Modest","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0415,"intrinsic_sd":0.4437,"effect_this_season":0.2166,"effect_ratio":0.4882,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.8528,"p_below":0.013,"p_near":0.109,"p_above":0.878,"forecast_words":"Likely (88%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":7.4582,"values":[18.14,17.786,17.433,18.264,18.491,18.205,17.98,18.919,19.054,18.98,19.366,18.222,17.875,18.138,17.826,19.217,19.072,18.628,18.039,18.87,19.213,18.32,19.32,18.909,19.563,18.627,18.739,18.046,18.252,18.972,19.572,19.42,19.224,19.077,18.783,19.057,19.448,20.268,18.386,18.773,19.406,19.162,18.118,19.594,19.288,19.273,19.892,19.311,19.611,18.848,19.371,19.443,19.791,19.502,20.067,20.11,19.572,19.52,20.084,20.094,19.949,20.189,19.767,19.685,20.461,20.1,20.219,20.546,20.276,19.445,19.841,20.0,20.099,20.38,20.33],"forecast_mean":20.5426,"forecast_sd":0.4757,"fit":{"a2027":20.326,"b":0.0985,"c":0.029,"tercile_low":19.4833,"tercile_high":19.9883},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.2883,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1331,"enso_p":0.0508,"confidence":"Modest","shift_this_season":0.2928,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.3027,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1052,"enso_p":0.0941,"confidence":"Modest","shift_this_season":0.2315,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.2549,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0476,"enso_p":0.4645,"confi